{"name":"Spinach Souffle","hex":"#83825b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spinach","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any member of species Spinacia oleracea of edible plants, or its leaves.","Any of numerous plants, or their leaves, which are used for greens in the same way Spinacia oleracea is or resemble it in some way."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spinach"},{"term":"souffle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of soufflé (“dish made with eggs”)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Alternative spelling of soufflé."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/souffle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spinach","blocks":[{"text":"Spinach is a leafy green flowering plant native to Central and Western Asia. It is of the order Caryophyllales, family Amaranthaceae, subfamily Chenopodioideae. Its leaves are a common vegetable consumed either fresh, cooked or after storage. The taste differs considerably between cooked and raw: the high oxalate content may be reduced by blanching."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Spinacia_oleracea_Spinazie_bloeiend.jpg/330px-Spinacia_oleracea_Spinazie_bloeiend.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spinach","wikidata":"Q81464"},{"title":"Soufflé","blocks":[{"text":"A soufflé is a baked egg dish originating in France in the early 18th century. Combined with various other ingredients, it can be served as a savoury main dish or sweetened as a dessert. The word soufflé is the past participle of the French verb souffler, which means to blow, breathe, inflate or puff."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Bacon_and_Cheddar_Cheese_Souffl%C3%A9.jpg/330px-Bacon_and_Cheddar_Cheese_Souffl%C3%A9.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Souffl%C3%A9","wikidata":"Q846376"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Illustration_Spinacia_oleracea1.jpg/500px-Illustration_Spinacia_oleracea1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Illustration_Spinacia_oleracea1.jpg/1280px-Illustration_Spinacia_oleracea1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Illustration_Spinacia_oleracea1.jpg/500px-Illustration_Spinacia_oleracea1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIllustration_Spinacia_oleracea1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Spinacia_oleracea_male_flowers%2C_spinazie_mannelijke_bloemen.jpg/250px-Spinacia_oleracea_male_flowers%2C_spinazie_mannelijke_bloemen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Spinacia_oleracea_male_flowers%2C_spinazie_mannelijke_bloemen.jpg/330px-Spinacia_oleracea_male_flowers%2C_spinazie_mannelijke_bloemen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Spinacia_oleracea_male_flowers%2C_spinazie_mannelijke_bloemen.jpg/250px-Spinacia_oleracea_male_flowers%2C_spinazie_mannelijke_bloemen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASpinacia_oleracea_male_flowers%2C_spinazie_mannelijke_bloemen.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Spinacia_oleracea_female_flowers%2C_spinazie_vrouwelijke_bloemen.jpg/250px-Spinacia_oleracea_female_flowers%2C_spinazie_vrouwelijke_bloemen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wiki